# CQ-14 · trait-crosstab
#
# Question: How many entities does the corpus carry in each animacy ×
#           countability cell?
# Persona:  P2 — scene-data annotator / ML researcher. The two axes are
#           orthogonal by design (§3.2); a cross-tabulation is how you check
#           that the corpus treats them as orthogonal rather than as a
#           relabelled single type hierarchy.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §3.2; §5.4 (`vso:animacy`, `vso:countability`); §5.12
# Form:     SELECT — one row per occupied cell
# Note:     Four of the six cells are occupied. An entity missing either axis is
#           absent from every cell — CQ-15 is the query that finds those, and
#           the two answers are meant to be read together: 39 entities appear
#           here and 41 assert an animacy.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?animacy ?countability (COUNT(DISTINCT ?entity) AS ?entities)
WHERE {
  ?entity vso:animacy ?animacy ; vso:countability ?countability .
}
GROUP BY ?animacy ?countability
ORDER BY ?animacy ?countability
